    "statements": {
      "intendedUse": "The reference material is intended for use in the validation and calibration of analytical methods for elemental analysis of copper alloys by ICP-OES, ICP-MS, spark OES, and similar techniques. Not for use as a primary standard.",
      "storageConditions": "Store in original packaging at room temperature (15–25 °C), protected from moisture and contamination. The material is stable under normal laboratory storage conditions.",
      "handlingInstructions": "Minimum sample size: 0.2 g. Surface material should be removed before sampling. The material is available as discs (approx. 38 mm diameter × 30 mm height). Follow standard solid sampling procedures for metal alloys.",
      "metrologicalTraceability": "Certified values are metrologically traceable to the SI via primary standards of the BAM and participating NMIs. Characterisation performed by 10 accredited laboratories using ICP-OES, ICP-MS, and spark OES. Homogeneity and stability verified per ISO Guide 35:2017. Uncertainties evaluated per GUM (JCGM 100:2008 / ISO/IEC Guide 98-3:2008)."
